          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#basic_idea Basic idea
          %p
            The basic idea is that a
            %em module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is an object equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          %p
            A familiar example of a module is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %em module
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            in the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            of abelian groups. Every element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            acts on the vector space by multiplication of vectors, and this action respects the addition of vectors, but nothing in the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            really depends on the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            or even a general
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
            %em module
            over the ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            An
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            can be thought of as a generalization of an abelian group, where the operation taking integer multiples of an element (seen as iterated addition) is extended to taking arbitrary multiples with coefficients in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %p This is the traditional and maybe most common notion of modules. But the basic notion is easily much more general.
          %h3#RelationToVectorBundlesInIntroduction Motivation for and role of modules: generalized vector bundles
          %p
            The theory of monoids or rings and their modules, its “meaning” and usage, is naturally understood via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} duality
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is to be thought of as the ring of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                on some
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %li
              %p
                an
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                is to be thought of as the space of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                on that space.
          %p
            A classical situation where this correspondence holds precisely is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
                theorem says that sending a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebra"} C-star algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,\mathbb{C})
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                with values in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
                constitutes an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                between compact topological spaces and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
                of commutative
                = succeed "-algebras;" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre-Swan+theorem"} Serre-Swan theorem
                says that sending a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff
                topological complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
                over a compact topological space to the
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,\mathbb{C})
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
                establishes an equivalence of categories between that of topological complex vector bundles over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and that of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+modules"} projective modules
                over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,\mathbb{C})
          %p In fact, as this example already shows, modules faithfully subsume vector bundles, but are in fact more general. In many contexts one regard modules as the canonical generalization of the notion of vector bundles, with better formal properties.
          %p
            This identification of vector bundles with
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            can be taken then as the very
            = succeed ":" do
              %em definition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            Gelfand duality is taken to “hold by definition” in that an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} algebraic variety
            is essentially by definition the formal dual of a given ring, and the Serre-Swan theorem similarly becomes the statement that the space of sections of a vector bundle over a variety is equivalently given by a module over that ring. (See also at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+module"} quasicoherent module
            for more on this.)
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} duality
            between geometry and algebra allows us to re-interpret many statements about modules in terms of vector bundles. For instance
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                of modules corresponds to fiberwise direct sum of vector bundles;
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
                of a module along a ring homomorphism corresponds to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                of vector bundles along the dual map of spaces;
            %li
              %p etc.
          %p
            Using this dictionary for instance the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            of vector bundles can be expressed in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+descent"} monadic descent
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+coring"} Sweedler coring
            for discussion of this point.
          %h3#more_general_perspectives More general perspectives
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            generalizes directly to that of a monoid in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %em algebra over a monad
            \. For more on this see
            %a{:href => "#MonadAlgs"} Modules for monoids in 2-categories: algebras over monads
            below.
          %p
            Apart from this direct generalization, there are two distinct and separately important perspectives on the notion of module from the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                modules may usefully be thought of in the context of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
                (and the enrichment may be over a
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %li
              %p
                modules may usefully be thought of in terms of
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelianization
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategories
          %h4#MonadAlgs Modules for monoids in 2-categories: modules over monads
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            generalizes straightforwardly from monoids in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            to monoids in a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monad"} module over a monad
            (see there for more details) is defined essentially exactly as that of module over a monoid. For historical reasons, a module over a monad in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            is called an
            = succeed "," do
              %em algebra over a monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+algebra"} universal algebra
            can be obtained as algebras/modules over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitary+monad"} finitary monad
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            forgetful functor are exactly algebras of that type. Modules over a fixed monad (in
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            of the monad; in an arbitrary bicategory, this category generalized to Eilenberg-Moore objects which may or may not exist.
          %h4#enriched_presheaves Enriched presheaves
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+an+enriched+category"} module over an enriched category
          %h4#stabilized_overcategories Stabilized overcategories
          %p
            A module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            over a (commutative, unital) ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            may be encoded in another ring: the one that as an abelian group is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus N
            and whose product is defined by the formulas
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (r_1, n_1) \cdot (r_2,n_2) := (r_1 r_2, r_2 n_1 + r_1 n_2)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is a
            %strong square-0 extension
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus N \to R
            which is the identity on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and sends all elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            to 0. As such,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus N \to R
            is an object in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing/R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing/R
            = succeed "!)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
          %p
            From this perspective, it makes sense for general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to think of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelianization
            of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/A
            as categories of modules over the object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Taken all together, this makes the fiberwise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelianization
            of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cod
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod : [I,C] \to C
            the category of all possible modules over all objects of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            This general perspective has a nice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} vertical categorification
            to the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            in this context, and the fiberwise stabilization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_C \to C
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sAlg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sAlg_k
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+ring"} simplicial algebras
            over a ground field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            of characteristic 0, we have that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi sAlgk
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(sAlgk/A)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+quasi-category"} over (∞,1)-category
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is equivalent to the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Mod
            of
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h2#Definitions Definition
          %p
            We spell out the definition of
            %em module
            for
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ModuleOverMonoidObject"} modules over a monoid in a monoidal category
          %p Then we give more general definitions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InEnrichedCategory"} modules as presheaves in enriched category theory
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#DefWithOCat"}> modules as objects in stabilized overcategories
                \.
          %h3#ModuleOverMonoidObject Modules over a monoid in a monoidal category
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monoid"} module over a monoid
          %h3#InEnrichedCategory Presheaves in enriched category theory
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+an+enriched+category"} module over an enriched category
          %h3#DefWithOCat In terms of stabilized overcategories
          %p
            There is a general definition of modules in terms of stabilized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
            of the category of monoids:
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+modules"} Beck modules
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} tangent (infinity,1)-categories
          %h4#ModulesOverARingInTermsOfStabilizedSlices Modules over a ring
          %p
            The ordinary case of modules over rings is phrased in terms of stabilized overcategories by the following observation, which goes back at least to (
            %a{:href => "#Beck67"}> Beck 67
            ), and is found in the important paper of (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen70"}> Quillen 70
            ); both listed below. For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+module"} Beck module
          #Square0ExtensionsOfRingsAreAbelianSliceObjectsAreModules.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in CRing
              be a commutative
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
              of
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab(CRing/R)
              of abelian
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R Mod \simeq Ab(CRing/R)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We first unwind what the structure of an abelian group object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p:  K \to R)
              in the overcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing/R
              is explicitly
            %p
              The unit of the abelian group object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing/R
              is a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi Id
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    R &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; K
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{Id}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; R
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This diagram identifies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              with a ring whose underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus ker(p)
              of some ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              such that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in ker(p)
              we have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\cdot n \in ker(p)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus N \to R
              with itself in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              in the original category, hence is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi N
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus N \oplus N
            %p The addition operation on the abelian group object is therefore a morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi N
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi N
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi N
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    R \oplus N \oplus N &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; R \oplus N
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; R
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p With the above unit, the unit axiom on this operation together with the fact that the top morphism is a ring homomorphism says that this morphism is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi N
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi N
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi Id
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Id
                        %mo +
                        %mi Id
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi N
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R \oplus N \oplus N \stackrel{Id \oplus (Id + Id)}{\to}
                    R \oplus N
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since the ring product in the direct product ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi N
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus N \oplus N
              between two elements in the two copies of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              vanishes, it therefore has to vanish between two elements in the same copy, too.
            %p
              This says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus N
              is a square-0 extension of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            For instance the square-0-extension of a ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            corresponding to the canonical
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            itself is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+dual+numbers"} ring of dual numbers
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %h4#ModulesOverAGroupInTermsOfStabilizedOvercategories Modules over a group
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                of
                %a{:href => "#AbelianGroupsWithGAction"} Modules over a group as modules over the group ring
            %li
              %p
                of
                %a{:href => "#ModulesOverARingInTermsOfStabilizedSlices"} Modules over a ring as stabilized overcategories
          %p one finds:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group+objects"} abelian group objects
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice"} slice
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"} Ring
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+ring"} group ring
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Ring
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G Mod \simeq Ab(Ring_{/\mathbb{Z}[G]})
                    \\,.
          %p But there is also a more direct characterization along these lines, not involving the auxiliary construction of group rings.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group+objects"} abelian group objects
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Grp
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G Mod \simeq Ab(Grp_{/G})
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The proof is analogous to that of prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Square0ExtensionsOfRingsAreAbelianSliceObjectsAreModules"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G \to G
              with the structure of an abelian group object over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central extension
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              by some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              which more over is a split extension (the is the neutral element of the abelian group object) and hence is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product+group"} semidirect product group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi G
                      %mo ⋉
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G \simeq G \ltimes A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actions"} actions
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              by group
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              to carry a
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            This construction generalizes to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groups"} ∞-groups
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "infinity-action#GModules"} ∞-action – G-modules
          %h4#SimpRings Modules over a simplicial ring
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sAlg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sAlg_k
            (or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sAlg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sAlg
            for short) be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+ring"} simplicial algebras
            over a base field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi sAlg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in sAlg_k
            there is generally a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi sAlg
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A Mod \to Stab(sAlg_k/A)
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sAlg
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
            nor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+functor"} full
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            has characteristic 0, then this is an equivalence.
          %h3#OverHigherAndGeneralizedAlgebras Modules over an algebra over an operad
          %p
            There is a notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} algebra over an operad
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+an+algebra+over+an+operad"} module over an algebra over an operad
          %h3#multiplicatively_cancellative_module_over_a_rig Multiplicatively cancellative module over a rig
          %p
            A module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is called multiplicatively cancellative (in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#NazariGhalandarzadeh19"} Nazari &amp; Ghalandarzadeh (2019), Sec. 3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,s' \in S
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \neq m \in M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sm
                  %mo =
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sm = s'm
            implies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo =
                    %mi s
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s = s'
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#ExamplesOfModulesOverARing Of modules over a ring
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
          #RingAsModuleOverItself.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is naturally a module over itself, by regarding its multiplication map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \otimes R \to R
              as a module action
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \otimes N \to N
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \coloneqq R
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              More generally, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the
              = succeed "-fold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              underlying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is naturally a module over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi R
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi R
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi summands
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R^n \coloneqq R^{\oplus_n} \coloneqq \underbrace{R \oplus R \oplus \cdots \oplus R}_{n\;summands}
                    \\,.
            %p The module action is componentwise:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi r
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    r \cdot (r_1, r_2, \cdots, r_n) = (r \cdot r_1, r\cdot r_2, \cdot r \cdot r_n)
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              Even more generally, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus_{i \in I} R
              is an
              = succeed "-module." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
              This is the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              (over
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              The set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              serves as the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+of+a+free+module"} basis of a free module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi i
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in \oplus_i R
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combination"} formal linear combination
              of elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            For special cases of the ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Z}
              the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
          .num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-module," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion subgroup
          #VectorSpacesArekModules.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = k
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+of+a+free+module"} basis
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              holds.
          #RestrictionAndExtensionOfScalars.num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : S \to R
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction+of+scalars"} restriction of scalars
              produces
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* N
              from
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
              produces
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_! N
              from
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
          #SubmodulesInExamples.num_example
            %h6#example_8 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              a module and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{n_i\}_{i \in I}
              a set of elements, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} linear span
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi N
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\langle n_i\rangle_{i \in I} \hookrightarrow N
                    \\,,
            %p
              (hence the completion of this set under addition in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              and multiplication by
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submodule"} submodule
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
          .num_example
            %h6#example_9 Example
            %p
              Consider example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SubmodulesInExamples"}
              for the case that the module is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = R
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RingAsModuleOverItself"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submodule"} submodule
              is equivalently (called) an
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          .num_example
            %h6#example_10 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R \coloneqq  C(X,\mathbb{C})
            %p
              be the ring of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with values in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %p
              Given a complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(E)
              for its set of continuous sections. Since for each point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_x
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is a
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VectorSpacesArekModules"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)
              is a
              = succeed "-module." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,\mathbb{C})
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre-Swan+theorem"} Serre-Swan theorem
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,\mathbb{C})
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,\mathbb{C})
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              More on this below in
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#VectorBundlesAndModules"} Vector bundle and modules
          %h3#VectorBundlesAndModules Vector bundles and modules
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(E)
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)
            is usefully thought of as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of modules over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            For describing vector bundles and their generalization it turns out that this perspective of encoding them in terms of their modules of sections is useful. For instance the category of vector bundles on a space typically fails to be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that arise as sections of vector bundles one generalizes to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaf"} coherent sheaves of modules
            then one obtains an abelian category, something like the completion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect(X)
            to an abelian category. If one further demands that the category be closed under push-forward operations, such as to obtain a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            of generalized vector bundles over spaces, one arrives at the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaves of modules
            over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
          %p
            But it turns out that the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaves
            over a test space (see there for details) is equivalent simply to the category of
            %em all
            modules over the (functions on) this test space. This means that quasicoherent sheaves of modules have a nice description in terms of the general-abstract-nonsense characterization of modules discussed above:
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            our
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of of test
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
            our
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of “functions rings” on test spaces), by the above the assignment of all modules over a test space is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Mod : C^{op} \to (\infty,1)Cat
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Mod : U \mapsto Stab( C/U )
